WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.082
Moisture can affect airframes, electronics, motors, connectors, cooling, navigation sensors, cameras, and lenses.

00:00:06.082 --> 00:00:14.261
Water resistance varies by aircraft and configuration and must be confirmed through current manufacturer guidance rather than assumed.

00:00:14.261 --> 00:00:20.343
Rain adds water and weight, changes aerodynamic surfaces, obscures imagery, and reduces visibility.

00:00:20.343 --> 00:00:25.586
Snow can enter components, melt, refreeze, or hide the landing surface.

00:00:25.586 --> 00:00:32.506
Ice accumulation can change lift and control and should be treated as a serious hazard.

00:00:32.506 --> 00:00:36.910
Fog and low cloud reduce visual range and contrast.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:43.831
Aircraft lights may remain visible while obstacles, terrain, other traffic, and the route are not.

00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:50.332
Maintaining sight of one light does not mean the operation remains safe or compliant.

00:00:50.332 --> 00:00:56.414
Humidity, mist, and temperature transitions can create condensation on lenses or inside equipment.

00:00:56.414 --> 00:01:00.818
A fogged payload may produce misleading or useless data.

00:01:00.818 --> 00:01:07.739
Do not continue merely to complete a planned route when the sensor product has failed.

00:01:07.739 --> 00:01:12.982
If precipitation, visibility, or moisture exceeds approved limits, cancel or land.

00:01:12.982 --> 00:01:21.161
Protect equipment during transport and recovery, and avoid opening sensitive compartments in blowing rain, snow, dust, or spray.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:27.243
Wind-driven moisture can reach openings and surfaces that remain protected in calm conditions.

00:01:27.243 --> 00:01:34.163
Evaluate precipitation and airflow together rather than treating a light shower as an isolated factor.

00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:41.084
After exposure, power down, inspect, dry, clean, and document the equipment according to approved procedures.

00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:45.069
Address contamination or corrosion concerns before another flight.

00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:50.311
A normal landing does not prove that moisture caused no damage.
